entityDescription:
MIPRONS is a Start-Up, set-up in 2019, aims at developing innovative high-performing miniaturized space propulsion systems adopting water as a propellant which is &ldquo;split&rdquo; into hydrogen and oxygen through a water-electrolysis process.
In particular, 2 innovative space propulsion systems are under development and patent filed:
- &ldquo;Space propulsion system&rdquo; (PCT/IB2018/055595, already issued in Italy and filed in 49 countries), is able to deliver high thrust and high Isp (specific impulse), ideal to quickly accomplish manoeuvres such as orbit raising, de-orbiting, collision avoidance, etc, with low propellant weight.
- &ldquo;Low and high thrust space propulsion system&rdquo;, PCT/IB2021/061166. The second patent, a technological advancement of the first, refers to an innovative propulsion system, capable of delivering both low and high thrust (aka multi-mode), using water as a single primary propellant. Beside the water-electrolysis system there is a steam propulsion system for low thrust, ideal for high-precision maneuvering (attitude & control). In this way, it is possible to reply to all the satellite manoeuvres requirements (DV and RCS) with a simplified system (small, light and cheap). 
The systems can be installed on:
&middot; Satellites and/or their carriers;
&middot; Extra-atmospheric drones;
&middot; Final stages of launchers;
&middot; Small spacecraft mission services.
